Step 1: Start the program 
Step 2: Input two prime numbers p and q 
Step 3: Compute 
n = p × q 
Step 4: Compute Euler’s Totient function 
φ(n) = (p − 1) × (q − 1) 
Step 5: Choose public key exponent e such that 
1 < e < φ(n) and gcd(e, φ(n)) = 1 
Step 6: Compute private key d such that 
d = e⁻¹ mod φ(n) 
Step 7: Display public key (e, n) and private key (d, n) 
Step 8: Input message M (number form) 
Step 9: Encrypt the message using 
C = Mᵉ mod n 
Step 10: Decrypt the message using 
M = Cᵈ mod n 
Step 11: Display encrypted and decrypted message 
Step 12: Stop
